{"id": "x0177", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To make an old-f ashioned, you'll need whiskey, simple syrup, a dash of Angostura bitters, and ice. Start by adding two ounces of your favorite whiskey to a mixing glass. Add half an ounce of simple sy rup for sweetness and a few dashes of bitter s for depth. G ree at the mixture with ice until it's well chilled but not over diluted, then strain it into a rocks glass filled with fresh ice. You can garnish with an orange twist if you' d like. That ’s it—simple yet classic!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0185", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I think the most important thing large language models can do is help us understand and communicate with each other better. They can summarize long documents, translate languages, or even assist in writing stories and emails. By making information more accessible, they help bridge gaps between people who speak different languages or have difficulty expressing themselves. This can lead to greater understanding and collaboration across cultures and fields.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0193", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Algebra is a branch of mathematics that deals with symbols and the rules for manipulating those symbols. It involves solving equations, finding unknown values, and understanding relationships between quantities. The word \" algebra\" comes from the Arabic word \"al-j abar,\" which means \"re union of broken parts.\" This term was used by the Persian mathe matician Muhammad ib n Musa al-Khwariz mi in his book \" Kitab al- jabar wa-l-muqab ala\" around 8 20 AD. Al-K hwarizmi is often considered one of the founders of algebra as we know it today, although mathematical concepts similar to algebra existed in earlier cultures like ancient Babylon ian and Egyptian civilization s. So while al-Khwarizmi played a key role in developing the systematic approach to algebra, the concept has evolved over centuries through contributions from many mathematicians across different cultures.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 57, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0201", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The United States is in the Northern and Western hemispheres. It' s located north of the equator, so it's in the Northern Hemisphere, and it lies west of the Prime Mer idian, placing it in the Western Hemispher e.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
