{"id": "x0409", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, let' s break this down step by step. First, we start with 10 0 people applying for the job. Out of these, only 30% get interview s. That means 30 out of 100, or 30 people, receive interviews. Next, of those who are interviewed, 20% actually get a job offer. So, 2 0% of 30 is 6. That means 6 people receive a job offer. Finally, of those 6 people offered the job, a third accept it. One third of 6 is 2. So, 2 people accept the position.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0417", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 25, "onset_chunk": 24, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Walter collected $ 500 from his neighbors and another $1,50 0 from an online fund, which brings the total to $2,00 0 so far. His lawyer offers to donate three times as much as everyone else donates combined. So if we multiply $ 2,000 by 3, that gives us a total of $ 6,000 that his lawyer is going to contribute. That' s how much Walter's lawyer will give.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0425", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, so each box is 100 dollars and there are two boxes. So the total cost before discount is 2 00 dollars. Now, with a 1 0 percent discount, that's 20 dollars off. So the final price for both boxes is 18 0 dollars. Since there are 90 single-use contact s in one box, two boxes give you 18 0 contacts. To find the cost per pair, divide the total cost by the number of contacts. That means 18 0 divided by 1 80 equals one dollar per contact. So each pair of contacts will cost one dollar.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0433", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So each restaurant is getting 2 pounds, and there are 40 restaurants. That means they will use 80 pounds in total because 40 times 2 is 80. If we started with 200 pounds, then we just subtract the amount used from the total. So 200 minus 80 leaves us with 1 2 0 pounds of car rots that won't be used.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0441", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Janet had 2 2 green pen s and 10 yellow pens, which is a total of 3 2 pens. Then she bought 6 bags of blue pen s with 9 pens in each bag, so that' s 54 blue pens. And she also bought 2 bags of red pen s with 6 pen s in each bag, so that's 12 red pen s. Adding them all together: 32 original pen s plus 54 blue pens plus 1 2 red pens equal s 9 8 pens in total. So Ja net now has 98 pens.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 35, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0449", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The baseball coach spent $ 27 total, because 9 ball s at $3 each is 9 times 3. The basketball coach spent $ 1 12, since 8 balls at $ 1 4 each is 8 times 1 4. So the basketball coach spent $8 5 more than the baseball coach.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0457", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first movie is 1 hour and 30 minutes long, which is 90 minutes. The second movie is 2 hours and 5 minutes long, which is 1 25 minutes. Add ing them together: 9 0 plus 1 2 5 equal s 2 1 5 minutes. So it will take Max 2 1 5 minutes to watch both movies.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0465", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "John has 13 Lego sets, and he sells them for $15 each. So he earns 13 times 15, which is $195. He spends this money on video games that cost $20 each. If he buys 8 of them, that's 8 times 20, which is $16 0. After buying the games, he has $ 5 left over. Let' s check if the math adds up: 160 plus 5 equals 16 5, but he only had 195 to begin with. That means there's a small error in the numbers given. However, assuming the scenario is correct as stated, he sold all his 13 Lego sets, so he no longer has any Le go sets left.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 30, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0473", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Johnny took his allowance of 2 0 dollars and added an extra 10 dollars to it. That means he started with 30 dollars. Then he invested this sum, which triple d in a year. Tri p ling means multiplying by three. So if he had 30 dollars and it triple d, that would be 90 dollars. So after a year, Johnny had 90 dollars.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0481", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "On the first day, Slo ane counted 100 customers. The next day, she counted 5 0 more than that, so 100 plus 5 0 is 1 50 customers on the second day. Now, if the total by the third day was 500, we can figure out how many were there on the third day by sub tracting the first two days from 50 0. So, 5 00 minus 100 minus 15 0 equals 25 0. That means S loan counted 2 5 0 customers on the third day.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0489", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 22, "onset_chunk": 22, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, let's figure this out. Grandma Jones baked five apple pies and cut each one into eight pieces. So first we need to find out how many total pieces there were at the start. If she had five pies and each pie was cut into eight pieces, then 5 times 8 is 40 pieces in total. Now at the end of the evening, there were 14 pieces left on the table. To find out how many pieces were taken by the guests, we subtract the remaining pieces from the total. So 4 0 minus 14 equal s 2 6. That means the guests took 26 pieces of pie.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0497", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So we know that the two classes have a total of 80 students, and each class has the same amount of students. That means there are 40 students in each class. Now, in each class, 4 0% of the students are girls. Let' s figure out how many girls there are. If 40% of 40 is girls, then 4 0 divided by 100 is 0.4, and 0. 4 times 40 is 16 girls. So there are 16 girls in each class. To find the number of boys, we subtract the number of girls from the total students in a class. 40 minus 1 6 is 24. Therefore, there are 24 boys in each class.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0505", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 34, "onset_chunk": 33, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Mr. Heze kiah had 2 0 trucks carrying 20 tons each, so that's 4 00 tons total. But a quarter of the trucks broke down, which means five trucks couldn't deliver. That leaves 15 truck s working. Since each truck carried 20 tons, 1 5 times 2 0 is 30 0 tons. So the farmers got 300 tons of fer tilizer that day.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
