{"id": "x0705", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If more fish farms are built, the group most likely harmed would be C: people who sell fish from the wild. That' s because when there's a lot of farmed fish available, consumers tend to buy more farm ed fish and less wild- caught fish. This drop in demand for wild-caught fish hurt s the income and business of those who rely on selling wild-caught fish.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0713", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 23, "onset_chunk": 22, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. The frictional force exert ed by the floor on the box. When you push a heavy box across a carpeted floor at constant speed, it means the forces are balanced. You're applying a force forward, but there's also a force backward due to friction between the box and the carpet. To keep moving at a steady pace, you have to keep pushing just enough to overcome that friction. Air resistance isn't significant for a box sliding on a carpet, the weight acts downward while you' re pushing horizontally, and gravity pull s down too, but doesn' t directly oppose your push in this scenario. So the main thing you're fighting against is the friction from the carpet.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0721", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 27, "onset_chunk": 26, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The term that best describes this activity is D, behavioral adaptation. The kangaroo licking its arms to cool down is a behavior it learn s or develop s as a response to the environment, not an inherent structural feature.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
